    "updated_at": "2017-01-24T22:11:38Z",
    "body": "There is createImageBitmap(canvas) that already exists as a nice way to grab a snapshot of the canvas.  However, the WebGL context will still stick around until garbage collected.  \r\n\r\nThis gives me another idea: we could add a dispose() method on WebGLRenderingContext to trigger an immediate tear-down of the rendering context.\r\n\r\nI think adding dispose() would be a simpler change to the API, it could be used to solve the problems that freeze() solves (in conjunction with createImageBitmap), and it would also solve the more general problem of zombie canvases hogging all the GPU resources.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
