    "created_at": "2017-02-09T15:46:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-09T15:46:48Z",
    "body": "So... what's the plan here?\r\n\r\nFrom a spec side, to me it seems like both freeze() and dispose() will be similar amounts of work, since they both require some kind of blanket \"every method on the context will now throw\" prose. (I guess a blanket statement will be simpler than inserting it into every algorithm, although people have a tendency to miss steps that aren't directly inside the algorithms. Maybe we should spec an extended attribute, [ThrowsWhenDisposed]?)\r\n\r\nShould we go ahead with speccing both? Just dispose()? What contexts get dispose()---all of them, or just WebGL? Similarly, does freeze() work on non-WebGL contexts?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/278680985/reactions",
