    "created_at": "2017-02-09T18:51:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-09T18:51:36Z",
    "body": "WebGL is the use case that really matters IMHO.  You can already get a 2D canvas to \"dispose\" its backing just by setting the size of the canvas to 0, and the context state does not really consume that much memory.  WebGL on the other hand can have plenty of big objects inside a context. So perhaps this API should be proposed against the WebGL spec? ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
