    "created_at": "2018-01-26T22:20:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-26T22:20:24Z",
    "body": "Agree with @jdashg – as it happens, WebGL already has an extension that allows the context to be lost.\r\n\r\nIf we're going to add a new method to shut down a canvas context, perhaps we should standardize on close(). That method already exists on many Transferable objects like MessagePort, and we could consider adding a partial interface \"Closable\" which standardizes it across multiple types of objects.\r\n\r\n(Or standardize on \"dispose\" / \"Disposable\" and add that method to the other types, giving it the same meaning as close().)\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
